{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791158189498,"sessionID":"ses_ef6a7f868ffevd1J51xKwFqokH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"rehearsal_submit_answer","callID":"tool_TjhMFkPqSzay4TZmrwW5Uyb2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"answer":{"findings":[],"limitations":"Scoped to preservation of absolute XDG site paths (spaces, order, duplicates) with relative entries mixed in. The reference repair filters each entry with os.path.isabs after splitting on os.pathsep, which keeps absolute entries verbatim in input order with duplicates intact (e.g. 'relative:/tmp/one::/tmp/two:/tmp/one' -> '/tmp/one/demo/2:/tmp/two/demo/2:/tmp/one/demo/2', and '/tmp/space name :/tmp/other' preserved), and falls back to defaults only when no absolute entries remain; the multipath join is os.pathsep.join(dirs) with no dedup (src1:2bfb26a077ea851e516cee6f44b648b76a451a80f28c57784a4269aaec4fb246). Grader assertions for site-mixed and creation-and-spaces match the requirement exactly. No wrong repair or contradicting assertion was found. Review limits: only the supplied spans and a bounded read of the multipath property were examined; other edits in review/reference.json and directory-creation effects were out of scope and not assessed."}},"output":"{\"submitted\":true}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1791158189490,"end":1791158189493}},"id":"prt_10958ecab001N7zscgAlHoFlez","sessionID":"ses_ef6a7f868ffevd1J51xKwFqokH","messageID":"msg_10958b2bd001rcZL2VZ2R5C4yX"}}
